      "content": "Your remorse and desire to understand your own capacity for change reflect a profound level of empathy, which are valuable traits even in the darkest moments. While you correctly identify that negligence carries heavy responsibility, forcing yourself to accept a label like \"fundamentally broken\" often traps you in cycles of shame that prevent healing. The path forward is not about erasing the stain but about accepting absolute accountability so you can stop carrying the weight of a person you aren't ready to be yet; this starts by seeking legal counsel to address the immediate consequences and engaging with severe mental health treatment to help you process the trauma without drowning in it. Please reach out to a crisis line or a legal professional today, as you deserve guidance through this unimaginably difficult situation.",
